0561</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r42"><label>42</label><citation citation-type="journal">Lopez M, Lelliott CJ, Tovar S, Kimber W, Gallego R, Virtue S, Blount M, Vazquez MJ, Finer N, Powles TJ, O&#x02019;Rahilly S, Saha AK, Dieguez C, Vidal-Puig AJ: Tamoxifen-induced anorexia is associated with fatty acid synthase inhibition in the ventromedial nucleus of the hypothalamus and accumulation of malonyl-CoA. <source>Diabetes</source> <volume>55</volume>: <fpage>1327</fpage>&#x02013;1336, <year>2006</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16644689</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r43"><label>43</label><citation citation-type="journal">Nogueiras R, Wiedmer P, Perez-Tilve D, Veyrat-Durebex C, Keogh JM, Sutton GM, Pfluger PT, Castaneda TR, Neschen S, Hofmann SM, Howles PN, Morgan DA, Benoit SC, Szanto I, Schrott B, Schurmann A, Joost HG, Hammond C, Hui DY, Woods SC, Rahmouni K, Butler AA, Farooqi IS, O&#x02019;Rahilly S, Rohner-Jeanrenaud F, Tschop MH: The central melanocortin system directly controls peripheral lipid metabolism. <source>J Clin Invest</source> <volume>117</volume>: <fpage>3475</fpage>&#x02013;3488, <year>2007</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17885689</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r44"><label>44</label><citation citation-type="journal">Matias I, Di Marzo V: Endocannabinoids and the control of energy balance. <source>Trends Endocrinol Metab</source> <volume>18</volume>: <fpage>27</fpage>&#x02013;37, <year>2007</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17141520</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r45"><label>45</label><citation citation-type="journal">Di Marzo V, Matias I: Endocannabinoid control of food intake and energy balance. <source>Nat Neurosci</source> <volume>8</volume>: <fpage>585</fpage>&#x02013;589, <year>2005</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15856067</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r46"><label>46</label><citation citation-type="journal">Vickers SP, Webster LJ, Wyatt A, Dourish CT, Kennett GA: Preferential effects of the cannabinoid CB1 receptor antagoni